note <A call to an asynchronous task on the right of an operator is awaited after the left operand ran>

# Item 1678 (T-1671). A call to an asynchronous task stands on the right of an operator (`is-equal`, `is-below`,
# `add`, `and`, `or`) as it stands anywhere else: awaited with nothing written, after the left operand ran, and under
# `and` and `or` only when the left lets it run. Each call writes its word at the end of a log, so the log is the
# order the calls ran in. swiftc refuses `x == await f()`: Swift writes the awaited operand in parentheses, and the
# right of `&&` and `||` (an autoclosure, which cannot await) as the branch of a conditional (swift-emit.tree
# emit-binary). TypeScript, Rust and Kotlin await in place. Held by `pnpm term:base-gate`.

# the word, after it is written at the end of the log
task logged
  mark async
  take log, like list, like text
  take word, like text
  like text
  call log/push
    read word
  send back, read word

# the number, after its digits are written at the end of the log
task counted
  mark async
  take log, like list, like text
  take size, like integer
  like integer
  call log/push
    text <{{size}}>
  send back, read size

# the flag as given, known only when the program runs, so no `and` or `or` over it is folded away
task given
  mark async
  take flag, like boolean
  like boolean
  send back, read flag

test <an awaited call on the right of is-equal is compared after the left operand ran>
  save log
    make list
  save word, text <left>
  save same
    call is-equal
      call logged
        read log
        text <left>
      call logged
        read log
        text <right>
  save plain
    call is-equal
      read word
      call logged
        read log
        text <left>
  want hold
    call and
      call and
        call not
          read same
        read plain
      call is-equal
        call log/join
          text <,>
        text <left,right,left>

test <an awaited call on the right of is-below and add is a number like any other>
  save log
    make list
  save below
    call is-below
      call counted
        read log
        code 1
      call counted
        read log
        code 2
  save sum
    call add
      code 40
      call counted
        read log
        code 2
  want hold
    call and
      call and
        read below
        call is-equal
          read sum
          code 42
      call is-equal
        call log/join
          text <,>
        text <1,2,2>

test <an awaited call on the right of and and or runs only when the left lets it>
  save log
    make list
  save yes
    call given
      true
  save no
    call given
      false
  save both
    call and
      read yes
      call is-equal
        call logged
          read log
          text <and-ran>
        text <and-ran>
  save skipped
    call and
      read no
      call is-equal
        call logged
          read log
          text <and-skipped>
        text <and-skipped>
  save either
    call or
      read no
      call is-equal
        call logged
          read log
          text <or-ran>
        text <or-ran>
  save held
    call or
      read yes
      call is-equal
        call logged
          read log
          text <or-skipped>
        text <or-skipped>
  want hold
    call and
      call and
        call and
          read both
          call not
            read skipped
        call and
          read either
          read held
      call is-equal
        call log/join
          text <,>
        text <and-ran,or-ran>
